WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
Three async streams

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:03.333
tame Apple's oldest-feeling

00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:04.371
Bluetooth API

00:00:04.902 --> 00:00:06.246
CoreBluetooth is one

00:00:06.058 --> 00:00:07.295
of the oldest-feeling

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:08.404
APIs an iOS

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:09.678
developer still uses

00:00:09.761 --> 00:00:11.199
with everything arriving

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.555
through delegate callbacks

00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:13.986
The author built

00:00:13.797 --> 00:00:14.905
Pulse a small

00:00:14.717 --> 00:00:16.427
SwiftUI app that

00:00:16.238 --> 00:00:17.205
reads live heart

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:17.983
rate from any

00:00:17.795 --> 00:00:19.021
chest strap or

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:19.646
watch using the

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:20.625
standard Bluetooth

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:21.651
Heart Rate service

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:22.838
He put a

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.406
Swift Concurrency API

00:00:24.218 --> 00:00:24.937
in front of

00:00:24.749 --> 00:00:25.102
it

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:26.399
with three async

00:00:26.211 --> 00:00:27.779
streams for availability

00:00:28.015 --> 00:00:29.796
scanning and connecting

00:00:29.973 --> 00:00:30.715
so the rest

00:00:30.527 --> 00:00:31.116
of the app

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:31.859
never sees a

00:00:31.671 --> 00:00:32.414
delegate

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:33.948
Full story on

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:34.655
the dashboard
